🔥 3️⃣3️⃣ Very Important GATE Trap

Don't say:

> "TCP always doubles cwnd every RTT."



❌ Not always.

It approximately doubles during slow start, subject to implementation details and ACK behavior.

During congestion avoidance:

\[
\boxed{\text{approximately linear growth}}
\]


---

3️⃣4️⃣ Another Important Trap

Don't confuse:

rwnd

with:

cwnd

rwnd

Receiver tells sender:

> "How much more can I receive?"



cwnd

TCP sender's congestion control says:

> "How much should I allow into the network?"




